# UST.G3BM Correction-Direction First Toric Return Theorem v1

## Result

Freeze the exact 18-term G3BI correction direction compiled by G3BK and specialize it at the selected proof fiber `(p,gamma)=(11,3)`. Apply the frozen targeted pole-six transform to every one of the 248 H02 residue-basis sources, then perform exact toric reduction in the complete H02 ambient degree.

The resulting first-return block has the exact finite-field invariants

```text
shape                 248 x 248
rank over GF(11)      248
determinant mod 11    7
nonzero entries       56,032
```

Thus the correction-induced H02 first return is an isomorphism at the selected proof fiber. This is a new calculation for the G3BI correction source; it is not a relabeling of the previously closed generic H02 block.

The computation also emits the complete `42706 x 248` ambient return with `2,778,007` nonzero entries, together with a solver-ready exact CSC right-hand side. The retained lower-pole quotient data has 1,076 distinct Groebner generators in its support and 5,462,541 coefficient terms with multiplicity.

## Exact scope

